A crown–rump length ultrasound shows a grayscale first‑trimester scan with a small curved fetal pole inside a round gestational sac, caliper markers and a straight measurement line between crown and rump
A crown–rump length ultrasound shows a small curved fetal silhouette within a rounded gestational sac, grayscale grainy texture, caliper markers or measurement line spanning head to rump, varying orientations,
Gray-scale sagittal ultrasound showing a small curved fetal silhouette from crown to rump, often with caliper lines and numeric CRL measurement; images vary in magnification, contrast, fetal position,
Sagittal grayscale ultrasound shows a small curved fetal pole within a rounded gestational sac, echogenic cranial and trunk outlines connected by a hypoechoic space, with caliper lines and numeric Crown–Rump Length measurement
Grayscale sagittal fetal image showing a curved embryonic pole within the gestational sac, variable curvature and size, echogenic cranial and caudal margins, superimposed caliper line measuring crown-to-rump length,
Crown‑rump length ultrasound images show a grayscale, sagittal fetal silhouette curled within a gestational sac, with electronic calipers marking crown and rump ends and a numeric measurement;
Crown rump length ultrasound images display a grayscale sagittal or transverse fetal silhouette with a curved head-to-torso axis, bright fetal outline, measurement calipers along the longest axis,
First-trimester crown-rump length ultrasound images show a small curved fetal silhouette within a gestational sac, grayscale textures, a bright echogenic rim, caliper markers and a measurement line; include fetal curvature,
A crown–rump length ultrasound shows a grayscale sagittal fetal profile with a curved soft-tissue contour from rounded head to rump, surrounding anechoic fluid, plus measurement calipers or a linear ruler;
Grayscale ultrasound shows a small curved fetal pole within a rounded gestational sac, often with caliper markers spanning crown to rump; images vary in magnification, contrast, probe angle and clarity,
